From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
Subject: [PATCH] xilinx_dsp: initialize pattern-detect parameter

The Xilinx DSP pattern matcher reads USE_PATTERN_DETECT from DSP48E1 cells,
including cells inferred before addDsp() creates new cells. Such cells may not
carry the optional parameter, so Yosys aborts with "Accessing non existing
parameter \\USE_PATTERN_DETECT". Initialize new cells and normalize existing
XC7 DSP cells before the matcher runs.

---
 techlibs/xilinx/xilinx_dsp.cc | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/techlibs/xilinx/xilinx_dsp.cc b/techlibs/xilinx/xilinx_dsp.cc
--- a/techlibs/xilinx/xilinx_dsp.cc
+++ b/techlibs/xilinx/xilinx_dsp.cc
@@ -47,5 +47,6 @@ static Cell* addDsp(Module *module) {
 	cell->setParam(ID(PREG), 0);
 	cell->setParam(ID(USE_MULT), Const("NONE"));
 	cell->setParam(ID(USE_SIMD), Const("ONE48"));
+	cell->setParam(ID(USE_PATTERN_DETECT), Const("NO_PATDET"));
 	cell->setParam(ID(USE_DPORT), Const("FALSE"));
 
@@ -810,4 +810,7 @@
 			// Match for all features ([ABDMP][12]?REG, pre-adder,
 			// post-adder, pattern detector, etc.) except for CREG
 			if (family == "xc7") {
+				for (auto cell : module->selected_cells())
+					if (cell->type == ID(DSP48E1) && !cell->hasParam(ID(USE_PATTERN_DETECT)))
+						cell->setParam(ID(USE_PATTERN_DETECT), Const("NO_PATDET"));
 				xilinx_dsp_pm pm(module, module->selected_cells());
